<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no test - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no test - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade quiet. Not enough slaughter steer or heifer sales confirmed for a market test.</p>
<p>Inquiry moderate, demand light. Sales confirmed on 100 mixed steers and heifers Friday.</p>
<p>This week's confirmed sales 62700 head including 17500 head or about 28 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>Bids Friday 63.00, asking 64.00-65.00.</p>
<p>Last sales of consequential numbers, Thursday at 63.00 for both steers and heifers of Select and Choice quality.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
